    {
      "id": "63bb8808-3892-5033-9f64-95fbaba813c2",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -704,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 736,
        "height": 1360,
        "content": "## Rotate on-call fairly with Google Calendar and Slack\n\nPicks next week's on-call person from the rota's own history, around leave and public holidays, and checks every swap people make by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every Thursday it reads the on-call calendar (the last weeks), the leave calendar and the public holidays for your country.\n2. It picks the person with the fewest on-call weeks lately who is not on leave, has no public holiday in their region, and was not on call the week before.\n3. It books the week in the on-call calendar, announces it in Slack and sets the channel topic at handover time. If nobody is free, the lead is told.\n4. When someone edits an on-call week to swap, the new person is checked against the same rules and asked in Slack. If they confirm, the swap stands; if not, or if it breaks a rule, the week is put back.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a Google Calendar credential and a Slack credential.\n2. Create an on-call calendar and a leave calendar, and pick them in the calendar nodes.\n3. Fill **Rota Rules**: one team member per line as `Name; region; Slack member ID`, your country and the lead's Slack ID.\n4. Pick the Slack channel in the Slack nodes.\n\n### Good to know\nLeave counts for a person when the leave event's title contains their name.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
